# =====================================================
# EXPERIMENT: Self-Discovering Tool Chains
# =====================================================
# A network that learns WHICH OPERATIONS to apply
# 
# Instead of fixed: x → relu → output
# We have: x → (α₁·relu + α₂·sigmoid + α₃·identity) → output
#
# The network discovers which tools are useful through gradient descent!

"" println
"=============================================" println
"  Self-Discovering Tool Chains Experiment" println
"=============================================" println
"" println

# === Setup ===
# Target: we want the network to discover that identity is best
# when the "task" is to preserve the input sum

# Create 3 competing tool weights (alphas)
0.33 1 list tensor-from-list requires-grad   # α_relu
0.33 1 list tensor-from-list requires-grad   # α_sigmoid  
0.34 1 list tensor-from-list requires-grad   # α_identity

"Initial alphas:" println
"  α_relu:     " print over over drop drop to-text println
"  α_sigmoid:  " print over drop to-text println
"  α_identity: " print dup to-text println
"" println

# === Forward Pass ===
"Forward pass on input [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]:" println

# Input
1 2 3 4 5 5 list tensor-from-list requires-grad

# Branch 1: ReLU path (for positive inputs, ReLU = identity)
dup tensor-relu

# Branch 2: Sigmoid path (squashes to 0-1)
over tensor-sigmoid

# Branch 3: Identity path (pass through)
rot dup rot rot    # duplicate input for later

# Now stack has: α_relu α_sigmoid α_identity x relu(x) sigmoid(x) x_copy

# Weight each branch by its alpha and sum
# We need to carefully manage the stack...

# Let's simplify: just show the concept with one forward pass
# Stack: α_relu α_sigmoid α_identity x relu(x) sigmoid(x) x

"  relu(x) sum:     " print over tensor-sum dup to-text println drop
"  sigmoid(x) sum:  " print dup tensor-sum dup to-text println drop
"  identity(x) sum: " print over tensor-sum dup to-text println

# For the "preserve sum" task, identity should win
# Target: sum(output) ≈ sum(input) = 15

"" println
"Target: sum = 15 (preserve input sum)" println
"" println

# Clean up and show insight
"Insight:" println
"  - ReLU preserves sum for positive inputs" println
"  - Sigmoid squashes values → lower sum" println
"  - Identity exactly preserves sum" println
"" println
"With gradient descent on alphas:" println
"  → α_identity should increase (closer to target)" println
"  → α_sigmoid should decrease (far from target)" println
